        "original_id": "fddcd93d-1758-5dc4-a20a-3f81a1e5e708",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: None\n- Concepts: plant taxonomy, genera, species counts\n- Organizations: None\n- Topics: Centaurium, Dacrydium, Schenkia, Gentianaceae, Podocarpaceae\n\nFacts:\n- Centaurium, also called centaury, is a genus of 20 species in the gentian family Gentianaceae, tribe Chironieae, subtribe Chironiinae.\n- Dacrydium is a genus of conifers in the podocarp family Podocarpaceae.\n- Dacrydium currently includes 16 recognized species of evergreen dioecious trees and shrubs.\n- Schenkia is sometimes included in the genus Centaurium.",
